<section id="how" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl scroll-mt-20 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6">
  <h2 class="reveal text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">How it works</h2>
  <div class="reveal mt-10 flex flex-col gap-4 md:flex-row md:items-stretch" style="--d: 60ms">
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel p-4 font-mono text-xs md:w-64">
      <p class="font-semibold text-cream">your terminal</p>
      <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-fog">
        keystrokes in<br />ANSI frames out<br />repaints on resize
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1 md:flex-1 md:flex-row md:gap-2" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-fog">stdout · escapes</span>
      <span class="hidden h-px flex-1 bg-line md:block"></span>
      <span class="text-fog max-md:rotate-90">▸</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel p-4 font-mono text-xs md:w-72">
      <p class="font-semibold text-teal">mimon engine</p>
      <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-fog">
        127.0.0.1:7800<br />agent loop · tools · audit<br />hard step cap per turn
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-1 md:flex-1 md:flex-row md:gap-2" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="whitespace-nowrap font-mono text-xs text-fog">your API key</span>
      <span class="hidden h-px flex-1 bg-line md:block"></span>
      <span class="text-fog max-md:rotate-90">▸</span>
    </div>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel p-4 font-mono text-xs md:w-64">
      <p class="font-semibold text-gold">model provider</p>
      <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-fog">
        anthropic · openai<br />deepseek · glm · gemini<br />any OpenAI-compatible URL
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-12 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="reveal">
      <h3 class="font-mono text-lg font-semibold text-cream">The render loop</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-sm leading-relaxed text-fog">
        The TUI writes ANSI escape codes straight to stdout. It measures every glyph — wide CJK
        characters and zero-width marks included — so boxes, prompts and diffs align at any width,
        and the whole screen rebuilds cleanly when the terminal resizes. The boot screen spells the
        agent's name in a hand-drawn pixel font, one color per letter if you want.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="reveal" style="--d: 80ms">
      <h3 class="font-mono text-lg font-semibold text-cream">The turn loop</h3>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-prose text-sm leading-relaxed text-fog">
        Each turn the engine rebuilds context from the session store, compacts history under the
        model's budget, and calls your provider with your key. Tool calls pass a permission gate —
        read-only runs free, writes and execs wait on a visible diff — and land in an append-only
        audit log. A hard step cap bounds every turn, so a confused run stops instead of spiraling.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
